{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/staffkind"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/staffKind","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"staffKind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Kind","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLStaffDetailsV4KindO","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<staff-type>"},{"text":" element.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"title":"staffKind","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"staffKind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Kind","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLStaffDetailsV4KindO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLStaffDetailsV9staffKindAC0F0OSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The kind of staff, such as ossia, cue, editorial, regular, or alternate."}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLStaffDetails"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLStaffDetails","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-details element is used to indicate different types of staves. The optional number attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies the staff number from top to bottom on the system, as with clef. The print-object attribute is used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to indicate when a staff is not printed in a part, usually in large scores where empty parts are omitted. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"is yes by default. If print-spacing is yes while print-object is no, the score is printed in cutaway format"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where vertical space is left for the empty part."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","title":"IvorMXL","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails/Kind":{"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Kind","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"MXLStaffDetails.Kind","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/Kind","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/kind","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-type value can be ossia, editorial, cue, alternate, or regular. An ossia staff represents music"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that can be played instead of what appears on the regular staff. An editorial staff also represents musical"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alternatives, but is created by an editor rather than the composer. It can be used for suggested"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interpretations or alternatives from other sources. A cue staff represents music from another part. An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alternate staff shares the same music as the prior staff, but displayed differently (e.g., treble and bass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"clef, standard notation and tablature). It is not included in playback. An alternate staff provides more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"information to an application reading a file than encoding the same music in separate parts, so its use is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"preferred in this situation if feasible. A regular staff is the standard default staff-type."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLStaffDetails/staffKind":{"title":"staffKind","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"staffKind"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Kind","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL15MXLStaffDetailsV4KindO"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails\/staffKind","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails\/staffkind","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The kind of staff, such as ossia, cue, editorial, regular, or alternate.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"}}}